      "block_id": "2605.25334_p5_b0",
      "text": "cues and 3D structural relations, respectively. The two query groups are placed after the visual tokens\nto form the full LLM input sequence [Fv, Qm, Qs, Ftq], so that both query groups can causally\nattend to the shared visual context. Whether Ftq appears before or after the queries does not affect\nthe design; we place it after the queries solely for notational simplicity. Since both query groups\nparticipate in the same causal self-attention at every transformer layer while pursuing heterogeneous\nlearning objectives, unconstrained attention from Qs to Qm would contaminate the structural pathway\nwith metric-depth signals. To prevent such leakage, we introduce a task-decoupled attention mask, as\nillustrated in Figure 3. Let [Sm, Em] and [Ss, Es] denote the index ranges of the metric and structural\nqueries in the input sequence. We modify the standard causal mask Mcausal by setting:\n",
      "bbox": [
        107.64,
        74.48,
        504.35,
        173.14
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        430,
        297,
